Z||000010||Wannabe||11-06-2000||11:25 PM||||Back in high school, a friend was driving with his mom in their Chev Caprice with a 350. The car was about 5 years old at the time. They smelled gas and a minute later noticed smole from the back of the car. They stopped and got out and within a few minutes, the car was engulfed in flames. Every once in a while, you will see a car fire on the road. Of all the fires I've seen, none has involved a Fiero. Fieros are not the only cars that catch fire. Didn't someone have a story about their Fiero being bunred to the ground when the mini van it was parked next to caught fire? Sheees. Anybody see the article in Car and Driver about how silly the Firestone hype has been? Witch hunts are still happening. They just come in a different form these days.||||reg||1
